	(text "Sensor 1 → PB6: Autonics PNP proximity sensor, PC817 opto input"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 22.86 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "cf3b3996-07b7-5614-b0b3-c2aa429c62c4")
	)
	(text "J10: 1 = +24 V (brown) through F7 100 mA PTC, 2 = sensor output (black), 3 = 0 V (blue).\nOutput ON (24 V): ≈ 2.3 mA through R32 10k + U6 LED → PB6 HIGH (3.3 V, emitter follower).\nOutput OFF, cable unplugged or broken: PB6 LOW (R33 10k pull-down).\nD18 1N4148W: reverse clamp across the opto LED. C18 100 nF / 50 V: supply decoupling + ESD.\nA shorted sensor cable trips F7 only: the other sensor and the board keep running."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 177.8 33.02 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "0f5882d9-1c3b-5d56-acda-b48fe69fe381")
	)
	(text "Sensor 2 → PC15: Autonics PNP proximity sensor, PC817 opto input"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 78.74 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "499d57a0-ad7e-5498-ada3-8fbceef69901")
	)
	(text "J11: 1 = +24 V (brown) through F8 100 mA PTC, 2 = sensor output (black), 3 = 0 V (blue).\nOutput ON (24 V): ≈ 2.3 mA through R34 10k + U7 LED → PC15 HIGH (3.3 V, emitter follower).\nOutput OFF, cable unplugged or broken: PC15 LOW (R35 10k pull-down).\nD19 1N4148W: reverse clamp across the opto LED. C19 100 nF / 50 V: supply decoupling + ESD.\nA shorted sensor cable trips F8 only: the other sensor and the board keep running."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 177.8 88.9 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "2d3ef08f-9a7a-5e61-9644-c10277b91ff2")
	)
	(rectangle
		(start 15.24 132.08)
		(end 297.18 175.26)
		(stroke (width 0) (type dash))
		(fill (type none))
		(uuid "c3ffc369-d50b-5ffc-a6c9-de8eae46d5b3")
	)
	(text "Sensor inputs: notes"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 134.62 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "eff465bc-4543-5d24-af1f-3b2ac8fcb17c")
	)
	(text "For 3-wire PNP (sourcing) 24 V sensors, e.g. Autonics PRD08 / PR series (brown +V, black OUT, blue 0 V).\nNPN (sinking) sensors need a different input circuit.\n\nSame circuit as the MES4-Flasher sensor channels 3 / 4 (PB6 / PC15), without the INA226 supply monitors.\nGPIO budget: all 14 module pins are used (Main sheet, MES4-CIF §2c). More sensors need inputs on\nI²C1, e.g. a TCA9535 expander (0x20-0x27), polled.\n\nPB6: the ST bootloader enables a 25-55 kΩ pull-up on PB6 (blank chip only); with the 10k pull-down it\nreads LOW, which is harmless for an input. PC15: input only (RTC-domain pin, CIF rule 10): fine here.\nInterrupts: PB6 → EXTI6. PC15 shares EXTI15 with PA15 (INA226 ALERT): give EXTI15 to PC15 (sensor 2)\nand poll ALERT, which the INA226 latches (MASK/ENABLE LEN = 1), so no fault is missed.\nNo back-powering: the PC817 collectors run from +3V3_MOD (module finger 4), so nothing drives the\nmodule pins while it is unpowered."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 139.7 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "cc883058-b8c1-50d5-be75-328d35e1adae")
	)
